_dev/loop-engineering/phases-plans/proposition-final.md-384-## Execution behavior
_dev/loop-engineering/phases-plans/proposition-final.md-385-
_dev/loop-engineering/phases-plans/proposition-final.md-386-Node states: `idle, invalid, queued, running, waiting, succeeded, failed, cancelled, skipped, stale`.
_dev/loop-engineering/phases-plans/proposition-final.md-387-
_dev/loop-engineering/phases-plans/proposition-final.md:388:Run modes: complete workflow; one node + required upstream; **one node in isolation (sample-data stubs — see the dedicated section)**; selected nodes + required upstream; from a node through affected descendants; retry failed node; retry failed node + affected descendants.
_dev/loop-engineering/phases-plans/proposition-final.md-389-
_dev/loop-engineering/phases-plans/proposition-final.md-390-Cancellation is cooperative, reusing existing provider/export stop mechanisms where available. A cancelled run must not report success after a late worker finishes. Prevent simultaneous runs from corrupting the same project via a **per-project execution lock** with atomic promotion of completed artifacts. Preserve partial successful results when safe.
_dev/loop-engineering/phases-plans/proposition-final.md-391-
_dev/loop-engineering/phases-plans/proposition-final.md-392-### Caching and staleness (n8n's pin-data superpower — nearly free here since every step already persists JSON)
_dev/loop-engineering/phases-plans/proposition-final.md-393-
_dev/loop-engineering/phases-plans/proposition-final.md:394:Compute a node fingerprint from a canonical representation of: node type + version, relevant configuration, resolved inputs and upstream artifact fingerprints, and adapter/cache schema version.
_dev/loop-engineering/phases-plans/proposition-final.md-395-
_dev/loop-engineering/phases-plans/proposition-final.md:396:A cached result may be reused only if: the fingerprint matches, all referenced artifacts still exist and pass basic integrity checks, the previous run succeeded, and the user did not request forced regeneration. Graph/configuration/variable/upstream changes mark affected descendants **stale**. Persist enough information to explain why a cache was missed.
_dev/loop-engineering/phases-plans/proposition-final.md-397-
_dev/loop-engineering/phases-plans/proposition-final.md-398-Do not assume per-project artifact names alone make cache reuse safe — multiple workflows or branches may target the same project.
_dev/loop-engineering/phases-plans/proposition-final.md-399-
_dev/loop-engineering/phases-plans/proposition-final.md-400-### Error policy
_dev/loop-engineering/phases-plans/proposition-final.md-401-
_dev/loop-engineering/phases-plans/proposition-final.md:402:Supported per node, only where the capability permits: stop workflow; retry with bounded attempts + delay/backoff; continue through an **explicit error output** (a control path, not a data output containing an exception object); skip an optional node.
_dev/loop-engineering/phases-plans/proposition-final.md-403-
_dev/loop-engineering/phases-plans/proposition-final.md-404-Every failure includes: node ID, node name, stable error code, user-facing message, redacted technical details, attempt, timestamp, recovery suggestion.
