_dev/loop-engineering/phases-plans/proposition-final.md-507-- **Single authoritative registry** (Automa `tasks` object; n8n `INodeTypeDescription`): one contract drives palette + rendering + defaults + forms + validation + dispatch. Backend-owned here to eliminate frontend/backend drift.
_dev/loop-engineering/phases-plans/proposition-final.md-508-- **Schema-driven config with conditional visibility** (n8n NDV `displayOptions`): a new node is data, not code.
_dev/loop-engineering/phases-plans/proposition-final.md-509-- **Connection map + handle-encoded routing** (Automa `WorkflowEngine.init`): edges → `{source: targets}` map, O(1) next-node lookup; error branch = explicit fallback path.
_dev/loop-engineering/phases-plans/proposition-final.md-510-- **Deterministic ready-queue over raw stack** (hardened version of n8n `WorkflowExecute`): multi-input joins wait for all inputs; stable ordering makes plans testable; parallelism can be added later.
_dev/loop-engineering/phases-plans/proposition-final.md:511:- **Pin/cache upstream outputs for partial runs** (n8n `pinData` + partial-execution graph): this app already persists every step's JSON, so "run from here" is nearly free — but fingerprints + locks make it *safe*, not just cheap.
_dev/loop-engineering/phases-plans/proposition-final.md-512-- **Serialize minimal node shape** on save (Automa): documented persistent shape only, runtime props stripped.
_dev/loop-engineering/phases-plans/proposition-final.md-513-- **Typed edges carry real data**: the single most important property — it is what allows nodes to be connected, replaced, tested individually, cached, retried, and reused safely.

